      "title": "Modeling Inhibited Growth"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "82b83459-ec63-539f-a22b-a8c37cb9ae8c",
      ":question/problem": "The growth of the number of deer in a protected forest is directly proportional to the difference between its maximum capacity and its current population. Let $N(t)$ be the number of deer, and let $t\\ge 0$ be the time in years. If the maximum capacity is $179$ deer, which differential equation models this population? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "5205529e-d24f-5575-b17a-f204175bfbe6",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "baeef287-9f1e-546c-a319-6890e4d2c656",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-k(179+N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "52394db5-16e3-5a06-8507-2ea83a42be67",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-k(179-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "effb1b42-88a8-5ed6-9709-7f9009b05955",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k{N}^{2}(179-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "e890e21d-91ec-5ad2-ab1e-85a19ba1dcd1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(179-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "92cfce41-c422-5f5e-89c1-f0dd529b4576",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=kN(179-N)"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "e890e21d-91ec-5ad2-ab1e-85a19ba1dcd1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The rate of change is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the current population. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-N),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity and $k>0$.\n\nHere $a=179$ deer, so\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(179-N).\n$$"
    },
